RAPID
=====

Copyright (c) 2026 RAPID contributors.

This repository is the publication artifact for the RAPID paper. It contains
the RAPID reference implementation of the control logic (`src/rapid/`), the
experiment data behind the paper's tables and measurement figures (`data/`), and
the scripts that rebuild those tables and figures from the released data
(`scripts/`). All material in this repository is distributed under the MIT
License; see LICENSE.

RAPID is an independent method: it combines the Congestion-Aware Adaptive
Controller (CAAC) with Interruptible Proactive Draft Generation (IPDG). The
SGLang-based measurement harness and the early SpecEdge-based runtime prototype
used during development are not part of this repository. SpecEdge is one of the
eight comparison baselines in the paper's evaluation, alongside Fixed Budget,
Cost-Model (Online Speculative Decoding), OPT-Tree, SVIP, EdgeLLM, PEARL and
Sequential; the SpecEdge project is at https://github.com/kaist-ina/specedge.

External assets
---------------

SGLang and its dependencies, the model weights used in the experiments
(Qwen3-0.6B/1.7B/14B/32B, Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct, Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct), and the
benchmark prompt corpora (C4, WikiText, MT-Bench, OASST, SpecBench) are external
assets. They are not redistributed in this repository and remain subject to
their own upstream licenses and access conditions. The benchmark dataset
identities are recorded in README.md and in the dataset labels of
`data/runs.csv`.
